=================== erc721-uri-storage.adoc
     1	= ERC-721 Uri Storage
     2	
     3	The OpenZeppelin xref:erc721.adoc[ERC-721] URI Storage extension is needed to manage and store URIs for individual tokens. This extension allows each token to have its own unique URI,
     4	which can point to metadata about the token, such as images, descriptions, and other attributes.
     5	This is particularly useful for non-fungible tokens (NFTs) where each token is unique and may have different metadata.
     6	
     7	[[usage]]
     8	== Usage
     9	
    10	In order to make an xref:erc721.adoc[ERC-721] token with https://docs.rs/openzeppelin-stylus/0.3.0/openzeppelin_stylus/token/erc721/extensions/uri_storage/index.html[URI Storage] flavour,
    11	your token should also use https://docs.rs/openzeppelin-stylus/0.3.0/openzeppelin_stylus/token/erc721/extensions/metadata/index.html[`ERC-721 Metadata`] extension to provide additional metadata for each token.
    12	You need to create a specified contract as follows:
    13	
    14	[source,rust]
    15	----
    16	use openzeppelin_stylus::{
    17	    token::erc721::{
    18	        self,
    19	        extensions::{
    20	            Erc721Metadata, Erc721UriStorage, IErc721Metadata,
    21	            IErc721UriStorage,
    22	        },
    23	        Erc721, IErc721,
    24	    },
    25	    utils::introspection::erc165::IErc165,
    26	};
    27	
    28	#[entrypoint]
    29	#[storage]
    30	struct Erc721MetadataExample {
    31	    erc721: Erc721,
    32	    metadata: Erc721Metadata,
    33	    uri_storage: Erc721UriStorage,
    34	}
